// @check
// @error unknown type 'nope' within '{[string]:nope}'
// @error unknown type 'nope' within '{[i32]:nope}'
// @error unknown type 'nope' within '{[string]:nope}[]'
// @error unknown type 'nope' within '{[string]:nope}|null'
// @error A boolean-keyed Map isn't supported yet
// @error unknown type '{[boolean]:i32}' within '{[string]:{[boolean]:i32}}'
// CONTRACT (must-error): a `let`/`const` BINDING whose annotation is a map with an
// unresolvable VALUE names the offending COMPONENT, exactly as the same annotation
// does at a PARAMETER (`unknown-type-names-the-component.vl`'s `d`), in a RETURN
// type (`unknown-type-in-map-value.vl`) and in a struct FIELD.
//
// It did not. The binding site alone printed the WHOLE spelling — `unknown type
// '{[string]:nope}'` — because its unsupported-map-KEY gate probed the key with
// `nameToTy`, whose wrapper re-enters the `unkTyPart` bank at depth 1 and CLEARS it,
// erasing the `nope` the failing resolution had just banked. The probe now runs
// `tsLeafTy`, the leaf rung `tsToTyReal`'s own map arm asks: the same VALUE for every
// possible key (a key is a bare `IDENT`, so `nameToTy` runs `primTyOfName` →
// `tpEnvTyOfName` → `declaredTyOfName`, which IS `tsLeafTy`) and no bank side effect.
// A diagnostic probe has no business perturbing a diagnostic bank.
//
// The last two lines are the LIFETIME boundary this must not break, and they are the
// reason the key gate exists at all:
//   · an UNSUPPORTED KEY still takes the actionable capability message, not the bank's
//     — nothing failed at a leaf inside it, and it must not inherit a `nope` banked
//     above (`unknown-type-names-the-component.vl` is the reset's other witness);
//   · a supported key wrapping an unsupported one (`{[string]: {[boolean]: i32}}`)
//     names the INNER MAP — the component — which is the whole point of the bank.
const _a: {[string]: nope} = Map()
const _b: {[i32]: nope} = Map()
const _c: {[string]: nope}[] = []
const _d: {[string]: nope} | null = null
const _e: {[boolean]: i32} = Map()
const _f: {[string]: {[boolean]: i32}} = Map()
print(0)
